  "body": "Follow-ups from the high-tier review of PR #810 (#804, A-index swept radius): https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/810#pullrequestreview-5856456980\n\n1. **A rotary with no `axis` vector isn't judged** (`crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs:47`). A custom work-turning A whose `.mch` states no axis vector posts `G0 A..` with no swing check, a silent pass. Either treat an A with no stated axis as about X (with the ISO default), or refuse it by name. Pin it.\n2. **The changelog row should say custom machines now refuse:** a user's table-A `.mch` without `nose_to_axis` now has every op refused by name, which is a visible behaviour change.\n3. **Projects saved before #810** that embed a user's own table-A machine have no `turns_part`, so they stay unjudged until the machine is reloaded. Show a load-time note telling the user to reload the machine.\n4. **README (tester kit):** state that the check assumes the stored G30 Z is at the top of travel.\n\nEffort: high (a post-gate safety law).\n\n**Done means:** an unstated axis vector is judged or refused, the changelog wording is fixed, the load-time note is in, and the README line is added. Each is pinned where testable.\n\nPart of #785.\n",
